const perspectives=[['I stepped onto the stage. My hands trembled, but I began the song.','a nervous performer','a sleeping visitor','a stage builder','From my seat I heard a strong opening note. I did not know the singer was nervous.','The performer knows a feeling the listener cannot directly know.'],['I checked the route before leading the walk. I wanted everyone to feel safe.','the walk leader','a bus mechanic','a book seller','I followed the guide and enjoyed the view. I did not see the route checks.','The guide describes preparation; the walker describes the experience.'],['I repaired a gap in the fence before the dog returned.','the fence repairer','the dog','a mail carrier','I saw a neat fence when I arrived. I never saw the gap.','Of these two narrators, only the repairer saw the gap.'],['I watered my plant every morning. Today a new leaf appeared.','the plant caretaker','the new leaf','a traveler','I noticed a leaf on the desk but did not know who watered it.','The caretaker knows how the plant was tended.'],['I packed three boxes carefully, checking the fragile cups.','the packer','a cup','a customer','I carried the closed boxes. I could not see inside.','The packer knows the contents; the carrier does not.'],['I practiced the poem alone until I remembered every line.','a reader practicing aloud','a person visiting the room','a person driving past','I heard the poem once and wondered how it was learned.','The reader explains practice the listener did not see.'],['I drew two plans before building the bridge model.','the designer','a person driving past','a river fish','I saw only the finished model and admired its supports.','The designer knows earlier plans; the viewer sees the result.'],['I placed a note in the library book before returning it.','the note writer','a librarian','a bus rider','I found a kind note from someone I had never met.','The writer knows the note origin; the finder does not.'],['I started the group task by asking everyone for an idea.','the organizer','an absent student','a newspaper editor','I felt included when someone asked me for an idea.','One tells the action; the other tells its effect.'],['I closed the window because rain was blowing onto my drawing.','the person protecting a drawing','a reporter','a painter outdoors','I noticed the window shut and thought the room was too warm.','The speakers know different reasons and effects.']];
reg('viewpoint4','Compare Viewpoints','관점 비교','4.T.C.2',(i,lv)=>{const r=perspectives[i];return lv===1?item(B('Who narrates this passage?','이 글에서 말하는 사람을 골라요.'),r[0],r[1],r.slice(2,4)):item(B('What difference between the accounts is supported?','두 기록에서 근거로 확인할 수 있는 차이를 골라요.'),`A: ${r[0]}\nB: ${r[4]}`,r[5],['The second account explains the first speaker’s private reason.','The first speaker learned the event only from the second account.']);});
const events=[['A child saw a lost hat and placed it at the help desk.','help the owner find it','hide it from everyone','keep it as a prize','The owner asked at the desk and got the hat back.','The choice helped return an item to its owner.'],['A builder tested a short bridge before making a longer one.','check the design','avoid building forever','decorate a notebook','A support bent, so she added a stronger one.','The test helped improve the design.'],['A class member asked a quiet partner for an idea.','include the partner','end all discussion','win a race','The partner suggested an ending, and the group used it.','The invitation changed the group story.'],['A gardener moved a pot into shade during strong heat.','protect the plant from heat','hide it permanently','stop watering','The leaves no longer wilted at midday.','The move changed the growing conditions.'],['A reader wrote questions on a card before a visit.','remember what to ask','avoid the visit','make an invitation','He used every question during the visit.','Preparation supported the interview.'],['A cook checked the ingredients before shopping.','buy needed ingredients','choose a color','cancel dinner','She noticed flour was missing and added it to the list.','Checking helped identify a needed ingredient.'],['A player practiced passing with a teammate.','improve teamwork','leave the ball at home','avoid teammates','They passed successfully during the game.','Practice supported coordinated action.'],['An artist saved a draft to compare with the new drawing.','compare the two drafts','hide every drawing','stop learning','The new drawing had clearer shapes.','Keeping a draft helped judge improvement.'],['A walker returned to the route after a wrong turn.','follow the planned route','get further lost','remove the signs','The walker reached the meeting point.','Correcting the turn helped reach the destination.'],['A student reread directions before gluing the model.','avoid a mistake','use all the glue','skip every step','She found that folding had to come first.','Rereading prevented a sequence error.']];
reg('character4','Choices and Consequences','선택과 그 결과','4.T.T.1',(i,lv)=>{const r=events[i];return lv===1?item(B('Which reason is best supported by the action?','행동에서 뒷받침되는 까닭을 골라요.'),r[0],r[1],[['keep the hat to wear later','lend out a hat without its owner'],['select a paint color','avoid testing the longer design'],['assign all decisions to one member','finish without the partner’s ideas'],['give the plant more direct sunlight','make the midday heat stronger'],['decide the visitor’s answers in advance','replace the visit with a written reply'],['buy every listed ingredient again','choose the shopping bag’s color'],['keep possession rather than pass','practice a solo shot instead'],['copy the newest draft','judge the newest draft'],['continue along the mistaken route','choose a different destination'],['glue before checking the fold','follow only a remembered step']][i]):item(B('How did the choice affect the event?','선택이 사건에 준 영향을 골라요.'),`${r[0]} ${r[4]}`,r[5],['The result caused the earlier choice.','The choice produced the opposite of the stated result.']);});
const stories=[['The first tower fell. With wider supports, the second stayed up.','Learn from a failed attempt.','Speed matters more than a stable design.','A fallen design should be rebuilt unchanged.'],['No one could carry the box alone. Together they carried it safely.','Working together can solve a problem.','A difficult task is best divided into separate attempts.','Choosing a smaller load is better than sharing a heavy one.'],['A promise was hard to keep, but the child returned to help as agreed.','Keeping commitments matters.','Convenience matters more than keeping a commitment.','Helping must be rewarded.'],['A hurried reader skipped a line. Rereading carefully made the meaning clear.','Careful attention can improve understanding.','Finishing quickly matters more than understanding.','Mistakes cannot be corrected.'],['The maker tested two materials and chose the one that held the weight.','Testing can guide a choice.','A material’s appearance is enough to choose it.','A familiar material is better than a tested one.'],['The visitor misunderstood a sign. Asking helped her find the room.','Asking for clarification can help.','A first interpretation is better than asking for help.','Questions prevent learning.'],['The team listened to an unusual idea. It solved a missed problem.','Listening to others can broaden solutions.','Familiar ideas deserve more attention than unusual ones.','Agreement matters more than comparing suggestions.'],['The musician practiced a difficult part each day until it became easier.','Steady practice can help progress.','Natural talent matters more than steady practice.','Practicing easy parts is better than tackling a difficulty.'],['A traveler expected an empty field but found a garden. She checked before describing it.','Evidence can change an assumption.','An early impression is better than later evidence.','Checking wastes time.'],['The child returned a borrowed tool even though it was still useful.','Respect others\' belongings.','Keeping a useful borrowed object is acceptable.','Borrowing transfers ownership.']];
const themes2=[['A: A bent support led to a stronger design. B: A torn sail led to a better fold.','A mistake can guide improvement.','The first design is usually worth keeping unchanged.','Changing a design is impossible.'],['A: Two friends moved a heavy bench. B: Three cooks prepared a meal together.','Cooperation can help complete work.','Independent work matters more than shared effort.','Asking for help takes away from achievement.'],['A: A reader returned a promised book. B: A player arrived to help as agreed.','Keeping a promise takes action.','Promises require no effort.','A reward matters more than a commitment.'],['A: A reader reread a missed line. B: A builder reread a missed step.','Paying attention can resolve confusion.','Speed is a useful substitute for checking.','Instructions prevent mistakes automatically.'],['A: A maker tested two supports. B: A cook compared two recipes before choosing.','Evidence can guide decisions.','A confident guess is better than a comparison.','The first option is better than a tested choice.'],['A: A visitor asked for directions. B: A learner asked what a word meant.','Asking can support understanding.','A quick guess is better than asking for clarification.','Confusion must stay secret.'],['A: A team listened to a new idea. B: A class invited a quiet partner to speak.','Listening can bring new ideas.','A leader’s idea deserves preference over a partner’s.','People must agree before speaking.'],['A: A musician practiced a passage daily. B: A player practiced one skill weekly.','Practice can support progress.','Progress happens without effort.','A brief practice is better than a regular routine.'],['A: A visitor checked a surprising scene. B: A student changed a guess after a test.','New evidence can change assumptions.','An earlier belief deserves preference over new evidence.','Testing cannot teach anything.'],['A: A child returned a useful borrowed tool. B: A visitor returned a found scarf.','Respecting ownership guides choices.','Finding means owning.','Useful things should be kept.']];
